<title>ITALY: SOCCER-PERUGIA COACH RELEASED FROM HOSPITAL.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PERUGIA COACH RELEASED FROM HOSPITAL.</headline>
<dateline>RAVENNA, Italy 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giovanni Galeone, manager of newly promoted serie A side Perugia, was released from hospital on Thursday with a clean bill of health, doctors said.</p>
<p>Galeone, whose job has been on the line since Perugia were knocked out of the Italian Cup by part-timers Nocerina two weeks ago, went to hospital on Tuesday with suspected heart problems.</p>
<p>But tests had revealed nothing.</p>
